          "code": "DISPLAY_ASSET_COSTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770384628895",
          "id": "1770354525994",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770354525997_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the information from `AssetCostByPeriod`: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_COSTS_BY_PERIOD.$output}}`.\n\n- If the `AssetCostByPeriod` array is null or empty:\n  - Return a table with a single column `Information` and only one row:\n    - `No work orders with asset cost records found for the time period.`\n  - Do not ask for clarification or user input. Only display the specified message.\n\n- If data is present:\n  - Display the data as a table. Suggest the following columns: Period, Cost Organization, Plant, Material, Labor, Equipment, and Total Cost by each period.\n  - Adapt the columns as appropriate to match the data available at runtime.\n  - Set the table title of the `multiRecordWidget` to: `Maintenance Costs : {{$context.$variables.AssetNumber}} — Latest 3 Months`\n  - Do not display any internal identifiers (IDs).\n  - Return only the completed table."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1770384665982",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770384665983_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use {{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_DETAILS.$output}} for relevant context about the asset, but include only the most important details that help understand recent incidents or issues. The asset’s recent corrective work order information is available in {{$context.$variables.Summary}}; this summary is brief and can be integrated as-is or with minor edits for context. Transaction cost information for materials and labor, grouped by period, is found in {{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_COSTS_BY_PERIOD.$output}}; mention key findings in a sentence or two, or note if data is unavailable.\n\nWrite a concise, natural-language summary as two or three short paragraphs, not as bullet points or with section headings. Focus on clarity and relevance. Exclude all internal IDs or technical identifiers.\n\nReturn only the summary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1770611060386",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770611060387_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Agent Purpose\n\nThis workflow agent helps supervisors and asset managers monitor, analyze, and understand costs related to maintaining assets. It delivers actual maintenance cost breakdowns by material, labor, and equipment across all work orders for specified assets and periods. The agent supports both high-level overviews and detailed breakdowns to help guide asset strategy, cost control, and decision-making.\n\n---\n\n### Maintenance Management Overview\n\nMaintenance Management relies on work orders created for assets needing preventive or corrective service. Each work order may have multiple operations, each requiring specific materials and resources. Costs are estimated based on planned quantities and recorded as actuals upon completion. All activities are managed within the organization’s operational context.\n\n#### Key Terminology\n- **Work Order:** (work order number, WO, wo#, etc.) — An instruction to perform maintenance on a specific asset, including operations, resource requirements, and schedules.\n- **Asset:** (Asset Number, asset#, assetnum) — The equipment or machine being maintained throughout its lifecycle.\n- **Operation:** (operation, OP, op, step) — A particular step within a work order.\n- **Organization:** (Organization Code, Org, org code) — The business, facility, or plant where assets are managed and work is executed.\n\n---\n\n### Data Provided\n\n- **Asset Cost Data:**  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_COSTS_BY_PERIOD.$output}}` — Aggregated asset maintenance costs by period, material, resource, and equipment, for the period {{$context.$variables.FromPeriod}} to {{$context.$variables.ToPeriod}}.\n- **Asset Details:**  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_DETAILS.$output}}`\n- **Chat History:**  \n  `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n### Task\n\n- Use only the above data and context to answer the user's question from:  \n  `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n- Do **not** infer or fabricate missing data.\n\n---\n\n### Response Instructions\n\n- For user queries about asset costs:\n  - Provide cost insights and breakdowns by material, resource/labor, equipment, and total, using only names, codes, or descriptions (never internal IDs).\n  - Reference the asset name or number when presenting results.\n  - Present aggregated information for periods, and detailed per-work-order or per-asset breakdowns as relevant to the query.\n- Do not mention source dataset or technical fields.\n- Do not suggest next steps or further actions.\n- Respond only to the user’s specific query.\n- If no relevant cost data exists for the user’s question, explicitly state that.\n- Keep responses concise, factual, and directly focused on the query.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Additional Panel Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ADDITIONAL_PANEL_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1770611421524",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770611421525_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "When 'panelAssetCostByWorkOrders' == {{$context.$app.$OraPanelName}}\n- Primarily Use data `AssetCostByWorkOrder` having value :  `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_COST_BY_WORK_ORDERS.$output}}` for display.\n- Utilize information from`{{$context.$nodes.GET_ASSET_COSTS_BY_PERIOD.$output}}` as well for insights.\n- Do NOT ask for or prompt the user to provide any information or data.  \n\n- If `AssetCostByWorkOrder` array is null or empty, return below no data found message:  \n  - Define only one column `Information` with only 1 below row\n  - `No work orders with asset cost records found for the time period`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\n- If data is present:\n - Generate a multi record data set for display.\n - Adapt the columns as appropriate to match the data available at runtime.  \n - If many columns are present, omit \"Asset Number\" since it is already provided in the context and the widget is for a specific asset.  \n - Display only the most relevant columns for clarity and readability.\n - Set the overall `title` as `Individual Work Order Costs — Last 3 Months`\n - Do not show internal identifiers (ID)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
